WEBVTT

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:12.960
Marilyn, you want coffee or tea?

00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:14.380
Coffee, please.

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:29.960
I am so excited!

00:00:30.380 --> 00:00:32.180
At this time tomorrow morning,

00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:35.040
Grandpa will be sitting in the kitchen with us.

00:00:39.940 --> 00:00:41.360
When does he arrive?

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:43.500
At six o'clock this evening.

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:47.460
No, by train.

00:00:49.640 --> 00:00:51.440
Are we picking him up at the station?

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:53.580
Not Grandpa.

00:00:53.860 --> 00:00:56.140
He doesn't want anybody picking him up.

00:00:56.800 --> 00:00:58.120
He likes to be independent.

00:01:03.180 --> 00:01:04.560
Great! Let's do it!

00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:12.480
We are going upstairs to set up Grandpa's room.

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:13.520
There's coffee ready.

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:19.100
I'm really excited about seeing Grandpa.

00:01:19.180 --> 00:01:21.760
Me, too. Milk, please.

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:24.060
He's so funny.

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:25.400
He always makes me laugh.

00:01:27.640 --> 00:01:30.200
I hope Grandpa's going to like living with us.

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:31.220
I think he will.

00:01:31.420 --> 00:01:34.100
It just takes time to feel comfortable in a new place.

00:01:34.280 --> 00:01:35.700
Won't he miss being in Florida?

00:01:35.860 --> 00:01:36.640
Well, he will.

00:01:36.680 --> 00:01:38.780
But I think he'll like being here with the family.

00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:40.260
Are you sure about that?

00:01:40.360 --> 00:01:41.960
It's crazy here most of the time.

00:01:41.960 --> 00:01:42.920
But it's fun.

00:01:43.060 --> 00:01:44.080
That's for sure.

00:01:44.980 --> 00:01:45.690
You know,

00:01:45.690 --> 00:01:48.340
maybe I'll put together some photos of Grandpa

00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:49.300
as a "welcome" present.

00:01:49.540 --> 00:01:50.820
That's a neat idea.

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:52.760
What can I do?

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:54.480
I've got it!

00:01:54.610 --> 00:01:58.150
I have a picture of Grandpa and Dad and me in my wallet.

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:02.380
at my junior high school graduation.

00:02:03.320 --> 00:02:05.300
Oh, I remember this picture.

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:10.320
I'd really like to pick up Grandpa at the railroad station.

00:02:10.970 --> 00:02:12.810
Railroad stations or airports--

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:15.300
Grandpa always tells us he'll get here by himself.

00:02:15.960 --> 00:02:16.780
He's something!

00:02:21.700 --> 00:02:23.820
Is this all Grandpa's stuff?

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:25.700
That's it.

00:02:26.340 --> 00:02:28.820
But I'm sure he has a few bags with him on the train.

00:02:30.800 --> 00:02:31.720
What's inside?

00:02:31.720 --> 00:02:36.800
I don't know. It's locked.

00:02:41.560 --> 00:02:41.900
Hi.

00:02:43.940 --> 00:02:46.620
I want to put some of my good hangers in Grandpa's closet.

00:02:47.120 --> 00:02:50.380
You know I'm very excited about his arrival.

00:02:52.660 --> 00:02:54.360
Susan called early this morning.

00:02:54.720 --> 00:02:55.460
She's unhappy

00:02:55.460 --> 00:02:58.840
because she's had to go to Chicago on a business trip

00:02:58.840 --> 00:03:00.000
and can't leave till tonight.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:02.040
She wants to be here for Grandpa.

00:03:02.260 --> 00:03:04.900
Well, Grandpa will be disappointed, too.

00:03:05.640 --> 00:03:07.020
He loves Susan.

00:03:07.280 --> 00:03:09.440
She always reminds him of Grandma.

00:03:10.180 --> 00:03:12.940
Well, how's everything here?

00:03:13.220 --> 00:03:17.500
Fine. We were just wondering about this trunk.

00:03:19.520 --> 00:03:20.680
It's locked.

00:03:21.460 --> 00:03:25.420
Oh. I have the key. Grandpa sent it to me.
